/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:148:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:149:Slide each foreground object horizontally to the edge indicated by whether its shape has an open notch.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:150:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:151:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:152:- Yellow is the background and there is one blue foreground color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:153:- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:154:- Each object keeps its row span and shape in the output.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:155:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:156:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:157:- If an object's bbox border contains a background gap flanked by object pixels along that same border, slide it to the right edge and recolor it green.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:158:- Otherwise slide the object to the left edge and recolor it red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:159:- Start from a blank background canvas; no moved objects overlap.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:160:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:161:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:162:- The target side is encoded by the object's shape, not by its original position: open notches go right, while closed or solid shapes go left.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:163:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:164:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:165:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:166:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="train" puzzle_id="d6e50e54" lines="8-25">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:167:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:168:Move each maroon marker toward the blue rectangle and recolor the rectangle red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:169:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:170:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:171:A background canvas contains one solid blue rectangular object and several isolated
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:172:maroon marker pixels. Each marker is horizontally or vertically aligned with the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:173:rectangle and lies outside it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:174:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:175:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:176:Start with a background canvas, repaint the blue rectangle red, and move each
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:177:maroon marker straight toward the rectangle along its row or column. Exactly one
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:178:marker is strictly closer to the rectangle than all others and enters the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:179:rectangle boundary; every other marker lands in the adjacent exterior cell just
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:180:outside its aligned side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:181:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:182:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:183:The single entering marker is the unique global nearest marker to the rectangle,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:184:not the nearest marker on each of the four sides.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:185:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:186:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:187:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:188:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="eval" puzzle_id="e87109e9" lines="68-83">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:189:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:190:Emit four teal beams from a square, turning at colored obstacles per a legend.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:191:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:192:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:193:- Top band: grey (5) legend with colored vertical bars in cells; bar position (left or right) encodes turn direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:194:- Below: main grid with bg, a solid teal (8) square, and colored obstacle blocks.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:195:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:196:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:197:- Remove the legend from the output.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:198:- From the teal square, shoot a beam in each cardinal direction (as a sliding copy of the square).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:199:- Each beam paints teal over bg cells as it moves.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:200:- On hitting an obstacle of color C, consult the legend: bar on left → turn counterclockwise, bar on right → turn clockwise. Continue in the new direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:201:- Beams stop at grid edges.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:202:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:203:Key insight: The legend's bar position (left vs right within its cell) is the encoding for turn direction at each obstacle color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:204:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:205:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:206:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:207:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="train" puzzle_id="e3fe1151" lines="36-55">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:208:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:209:Fill the one blank in each corner region so all four regions have the same color multiset.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:210:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:211:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:212:- The dominant background color forms one solid separator row and one solid
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:213:  separator column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:214:- The separator cross splits the grid into four equal rectangular corner regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:215:- Each corner region contains exactly one background-colored blank pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:216:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:217:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:218:- Count the non-background colors in each corner region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:219:- The completed region multiset is defined by the maximum observed count of
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:220:  each color across the four regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:221:- Replace each region's blank pixel with the single color needed to match that
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:222:  completed multiset.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:223:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:224:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:225:- The separator color inside a corner region is a missing value marker; comparing
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:226:  the four regions reveals the shared multiset without using numeric color order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:227:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:228:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:229:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:230:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="train" puzzle_id="6350f1f4" lines="62-81">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:231:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:232:Decode a block-grid image by swapping each sprite-coded cell with a solid cell and each blank cell with the sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:233:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:234:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:235:The grid is partitioned by black separator rows and columns into equal-size
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:236:square blocks. Each block is either a copy of one two-color sprite or a
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:237:uniform blank block of the sprite's minority color; grey pixels are erased
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:238:cells that act as wildcards.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:239:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:240:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:241:Infer the repeated sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks. Replace a
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:242:block matching that sprite, ignoring grey erasures, with a solid block of
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:243:the sprite's majority color. Replace a uniform blank block with the sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:244:Separator rows and columns, including grey erasures on them, become black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:245:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:246:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:247:The small sprite is a block-level code for one macro-cell state, and the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:248:uniform minority-color block is the other state; the output renders the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:249:opposite code in each macro-cell while cleaning erased pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:250:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:251:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:252:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:253:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="train" puzzle_id="c920a713" lines="87-102">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:254:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:255:Untangle overlapping colored rectangular frames into concentric square frames ordered by their visible crossings.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:256:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:257:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:258:- The background contains several one-cell-thick axis-aligned rectangular frames, one color per frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:259:- Frames overlap, and the visible color at an overlap records a directed crossing from the hidden frame to the visible frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:260:- Each foreground color still has visible pixels on the perimeter of its full rectangular bounding box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:261:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:262:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:263:- Infer each color's full rectangular frame from the bounding box of its visible pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:264:- Add a directed edge A -> B when B is visible at a crossing of A and B's frame perimeters.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:265:- Find the unique path that visits every frame color once, then render those colors as one-pixel-thick concentric square frames from outside to inside.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:266:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:267:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:268:- The output is not a crop of the input; the crossing graph gives a single frame order, and that order is redrawn as nested rings.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:269:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:270:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:271:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:272:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="train" puzzle_id="aaecdb9a" lines="10-26">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:273:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:274:Convert scattered foreground objects into bottom-aligned count bars in a fixed five-color order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:275:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:276:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:277:The grid has a dominant background color and foreground objects in the task
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:278:palette: grey, red, teal, maroon, and pink. Objects are monochromatic
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:279:8-connected components; some palette colors may be absent.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:280:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:281:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:282:For each palette color in order grey, red, teal, maroon, pink, count its
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:283:8-connected objects. Create a background grid with five columns and height
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:284:equal to the largest count, then fill each column upward from the bottom
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:285:with its palette color for that count.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:286:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:287:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:288:The output does not preserve object shapes or positions; it is a histogram
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:289:of per-color 8-connected object counts, using the learned palette order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:290:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:291:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:292:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:293:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="train" puzzle_id="9f8de559" lines="19-37">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:294:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:295:Erase the first border pixel hit by extending the red marker away from its pink trail.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:296:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:297:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:298:- The dominant background surrounds a unique red marker and a four-pixel
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:299:  pink trail.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:300:- The pink pixels form one straight 8-connected ray starting next to the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:301:  red marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:302:- In the opposite direction from that trail, the red marker faces a
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:303:  non-background border or obstacle pixel beyond background cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:304:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:305:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:306:- Keep the whole grid fixed except for the first non-background pixel on
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:307:  the ray from the red marker away from the pink trail.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:308:- Recolor that one hit pixel to the background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:309:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:310:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:311:- The pink trail marks where the red marker came from, so the edit is found
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:312:  by ray-casting from the red marker in the opposite direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:313:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:314:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:315:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:316:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="train" puzzle_id="6cbe9eb8" lines="79-94">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:317:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:318:Rebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:319:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:320:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:321:- A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:322:- The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:323:- A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:324:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:325:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:326:- Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:327:- Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:328:- Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:329:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:330:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:331:- The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:332:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:333:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:334:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:335:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="eval" puzzle_id="5961cc34" lines="8-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:336:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:337:Build a red ray network by activating blue blobs via directional green ports.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:338:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:339:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:340:- bg = most common color. Large blue blobs with adjacent green pixels marking port directions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:341:- Start marker: yellow pixel atop a short red segment at grid bottom.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:342:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:343:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:344:- Extend a ray upward from start; on hitting a blue blob, recolor it red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/prompt.md:345:- Activated blobs emit thick rays through green ports until boundary or another blob.
