/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:120:Recolor the small defect bars on each shared-color object with the opposite panel color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:121:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:122:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:123:- The grid contains two large panel colors and one shared object color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:124:- Each shared-color object is a mostly solid rectangle inside exactly one panel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:125:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:126:- Find the near-solid rectangular core of each object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:127:- Missing core pixels and one-cell protrusions define two-pixel bars perpendicular to the nearest core edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:128:- Recolor those bars with the other panel color; leave all other pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:129:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:130:- The colors to add are not tied to numeric ids: each object's surrounding panel identifies the opposite panel color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:131:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/3.md:132:<annotation>
