/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/2.md:305:Project maroon markers into adjacent grey or pink 3x3 squares, erasing grey squares afterward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/2.md:306:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/2.md:307:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/2.md:308:The grid has a dominant background, solid 3x3 grey and/or pink squares, and maroon marker pixels or segments directly touching one side of exactly one square.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/2.md:309:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/2.md:310:Grey squares are erased; their adjacent maroon markers stay in place and stamp the nearest edge cell inside the grey square. Pink squares stay pink; their adjacent maroon markers disappear and stamp the corresponding cell on the square's middle row or middle column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/2.md:311:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/2.md:312:The side touched by a marker determines the projection: grey uses the near edge, while pink uses the centerline, preserving the marker's coordinate along that side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/2.md:313:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/2.md:314:<annotation>
