/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:235:Extend each of two aligned rectangular marker objects toward the other, filling half of the gap across the full perpendicular span.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:236:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:237:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:238:- A dominant background contains exactly two solid, same-sized monochromatic rectangles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:239:- The rectangles share either the same row span or the same column span, with a background gap between their facing edges.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:240:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:241:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:242:- If the rectangles are side-by-side, color the left half of the inter-object gap across every row with the left object's color, and the right half with the right object's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:243:- If one rectangle is above the other, color the upper half of the gap across every column with the upper object's color, and the lower half with the lower object's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:244:- When the gap length is odd, leave the center row/column as background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:245:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:246:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1026159725/14/codegen_prompts/4.md:247:- The marker objects are endpoints of an axial corridor; their own size identifies the facing edge, while the filled corridor spans the whole grid perpendicular to that axis.
